# Kept out of the image build context.
#
# On the server the build runs inside the checkout, which is also where the
# live state sits: .env with every secret, the Postgres and Redis data
# directories, and the scans. Without this file `COPY . /app/` would bake all
# of it into an image layer, where anyone who later pulls or exports the image
# can read it - and a build would upload gigabytes of media every time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.prod.example
db/
redis/
beat/
media/
staticfiles/
celerybeat-schedule
docker-compose.prod.yml
docker-compose.override.yml

.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
